  "summary": "GitHub and GitLab can publish multiple markers for the same lane in one deterministic round when the finding digest changes. This violates the issue's one-marker-per-lane-per-round noise bound and inflates historical stats.",
  "blockers": [
    "Prevent changed-digest reruns from creating additional provider markers within the same lane round.",
    "Add or enforce idempotent replacement/skip behavior consistently for both GitHub and GitLab."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "issue-455-duplicate-github-marker",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "location": {
        "path": "adapters/github/src/github_review_forge.ts",
        "line": 661,
        "endLine": 678,
        "side": "destination"
      },
      "message": "The deterministic runId and round identify one lane round, but matchingCurrentLaneReview also requires the finding digest to match. A rerun at the same head and round with changed findings therefore publishes another GitHub marker instead of remaining one marker per lane per round; preserved history then counts duplicate blocking entries.",
      "suggestion": "Use round/lane identity as the provider mutation bound, or update the existing marker rather than creating a second marker in the same round; add a regression test with changed digest and unchanged round.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "id": "issue-455-duplicate-gitlab-marker",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "location": {
        "path": "adapters/gitlab/src/gitlab_review_forge.ts",
        "line": 643,
        "endLine": 651,
        "side": "destination"
      },
      "message": "GitLab's matching metadata likewise requires findingDigest equality after using the deterministic lane runId and round. Changed findings on a same-head rerun bypass the idempotency check and create another note for the same lane round, violating the issue's provider-noise bound and allowing duplicate history counts.",
      "suggestion": "Make same-round lane publication idempotent by skipping or updating the existing marker regardless of digest, and cover changed-digest reruns with a GitLab regression test.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
